{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_12_constitution_article_v", "label": "Article V \u2014 Contradiction is preserved", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-25-inferences.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_epistemic_ledger_poc_spec_v4_epistemic_ledger_poc_09_future_directions_s1", "label": "09 \u00a71 \u2014 Inferences and premises tables (deferred), CREATE_INFERENCE reserved", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-25-inferences.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_25_inferences_stage", "label": "Stage 25 \u2014 Inferences: recorded reasoning steps (implemented)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-25-inferences.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Asked for by the owner: \"Is this system capable of registering an inference like 'because A, B, and C are true and D is false this implies E is true'?\" It was not. A claim edge relates two claims and nothing joined several premises into one step, so a reader could not see which premise is the weak link or that two people reached E by different routes."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_25_inferences_create_inference", "label": "CREATE_INFERENCE \u2014 premises with polarity, type, rule, self-assessed strength", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-25-inferences.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two to twelve premises, each HOLDS or FAILS, with the warrant stated as untrusted display text and strength shown as a self-assessment. A conclusion among its own premises is refused; cycles across inferences are allowed and recorded because they are information (Article V), and no scorer ever follows them."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_25_inferences_not_evidence", "label": "An inference is never evidence and never touches a score", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-25-inferences.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Article III: evidence is what a source says or a measurement shows; an inference is what someone concludes from claims. So it carries no weight in either released model, the trace does not mention it, and traces are byte-identical before and after. A later model version may propagate belief; that needs cycle handling and a dependency model, and a new model version, never a change to an existing one."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_25_inferences_derived_from_edges", "label": "One DERIVED_FROM claim edge per premise, in the same contribution", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-25-inferences.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "So downstream_count, task priority and the existing edge display keep working without knowing inferences exist \u2014 the new object is added without a second graph to maintain."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_25_inferences_weakest_premise", "label": "The weakest premise, marked rather than computed into a number", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-25-inferences.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Inferences::View ranks premise states (supported 0 \u2026 contradicted 4) against the polarity the inference needs; a FAILS premise reading SUPPORTED is the weakest of all. No number is derived for the conclusion from its premises, and the section says so in one fixed sentence. `strained` inferences feed the weaknesses page."}, {"id": "implementation_implemented_stage_25_inferences_inference_review", "label": "INFERENCE_REVIEW task type, and the config it deliberately did not edit", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-25-inferences.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deviation from the plan: the released scoring configs were not edited to add its task_type_cost, because a config change would be a new model version (Invariant 4). Tasks::Priority falls back to the type's own cost for a type the config predates. Outcomes VALID, MISSING_PREMISE, NON_SEQUITUR, CANNOT_DETERMINE; a MISSING_PREMISE answer adds a claim and a corrected inference and the original stays."}], "edges": [{"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_25_inferences_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_25_inferences_create_inference", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-25-inferences.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_25_inferences_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_25_inferences_not_evidence", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-25-inferences.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_25_inferences_stage", "target": "implementation_implemented_stage_25_inferences_derived_from_edges", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "implementation/implemented/stage-25-inferences.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "implementation_implemented_stage_25_inferences_stage", "target": "implementation_i